Line 27: `(void)p; ck(pthread_mutex_lock(&returns)); ++stock;`
Line 28: `ck(pthread_mutex_unlock(&returns)); return NULL;`

Independent sales and returns locks do not exclude each other on stock. The ordinary counter has a data race even though both functions contain locks.

| Step | Thread A | Thread B | Shared state |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | lock(sales) succeeds |  | sales=A |
| 2 |  | lock(returns) succeeds | sales=A, returns=B |
| 3 | read stock for decrement |  | modeled old stock=5 |
| 4 |  | read stock for increment | same unprotected object; conflicting accesses |

